Done. `pipeline_refactored.py` replaces the original with every requirement addressed:

| # | Requirement | What changed |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Environment variables** | All config (`LOG_FILE`, `DB_PATH`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASS`) read via `os.environ.get()` with backward-compatible defaults |
| 2 | **Parameterized queries** | `load_to_db` uses `?` placeholders — zero string-formatting in SQL |
| 3 | **ETL structure** | `extract()` → `transform()` → `load_to_db()` + `write_report()`, each with clear single responsibility; `run()` orchestrates |
| 4 | **Regex parsing** | Three compiled patterns (`_RE_LOG_LINE`, `_RE_USER`, `_RE_API`) replace all `split()` / `in` heuristics |
| 5 | **Type hints & docstrings** | `dataclass` models (`LogEntry`, `ApiCall`, `SessionEvent`, `ParsedLogs`); full type annotations on every function; module and function docstrings |

